                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c12f09a2-3238-3aac-95ed-a98c31b32ab0",
                                        "entry_id": "99ce910e-1f1e-31fd-b69c-2e661e959fa3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Feeling or filled with remorse."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of a person"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f065eeae-c1d7-4157-93f8-21920ad3b2ea",
                                                "sense_id": "c12f09a2-3238-3aac-95ed-a98c31b32ab0",
                                                "text": "He was so remorseful that he voluntarily paid full restitution."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4f813f8e-2fcd-39bb-a488-8c58f18f70c7",
                                        "entry_id": "99ce910e-1f1e-31fd-b69c-2e661e959fa3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Expressing or caused by remorse."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f9f4c27-3554-43ea-9923-44f7a92e562f",
                                                "sense_id": "4f813f8e-2fcd-39bb-a488-8c58f18f70c7",
                                                "text": "There was a remorseful look on her face."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2437d9f0-37eb-41cf-a70a-5623ada82015",
                                                "sense_id": "4f813f8e-2fcd-39bb-a488-8c58f18f70c7",
                                                "text": "Quiet people too, for I think that about this time a sort of remorseful tenderness comes over the bullies and the nagsters, so that they go about gently and deprecatingly, hoping by one day's record sweetness to outface the year's blusterings."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d6e092a5-bc26-4588-b999-5918cc8304fc",
                        "source_entry_id": "4b5ed373-2d13-34b0-aa04-7eca8f10dd5e",
                        "source_sense_id": "965c368d-3daa-322e-9ce1-cef938a7745d",
                        "target_lang_word": "contrite",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "contrite",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4c9c0e57-8044-3be9-ad1b-9af96810a08b",
                                        "entry_id": "f9de688a-1ef0-321d-b305-96c75c486e22",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sincerely penitent or feeling regret or sorrow, especially for one’s own actions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a63e466-1a1d-4600-bd4d-f270169a094f",
                                                "sense_id": "4c9c0e57-8044-3be9-ad1b-9af96810a08b",
                                                "text": "The Lord will happineſs divine / On contrite hearts beſtow : / Then tell me, gracious God, is mine / A contrite heart, or no ?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea34b2fb-d1ed-4604-b7b9-d47c6ade3804",
                                                "sense_id": "4c9c0e57-8044-3be9-ad1b-9af96810a08b",
                                                "text": "He greeted Milo jovially each time they met and, in an excess of contrite generosity, impulsively recommended Major Major for promotion. The recommendation was rejected at once at Twenty-seventh Air Force Headquarters by ex-P.F.C. Wintergreen, who scribbled a brusque, unsigned reminder that the Army had only one Major Major Major Major and did not intend to lose him by promotion just to please Colonel Cathcart."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "47daa549-f316-3557-946e-40c235585104",
                                        "entry_id": "f9de688a-1ef0-321d-b305-96c75c486e22",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Thoroughly bruised or broken."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "contrite",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9545d21d-d12c-3a99-9645-014e954cb86d",
                                        "entry_id": "224a9ffc-306a-3513-ad01-39dc74519fad",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A contrite person; a penitent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31ff620d-2b3f-4363-880a-ca0a0011a1dc",
                                                "sense_id": "9545d21d-d12c-3a99-9645-014e954cb86d",
                                                "text": "Secondly, that even where contrition or inward repentance doth cleanſe without abſolution ; the reaſon why it cometh ſo to paſs, is, becauſe ſuch contrites intend and deſire Abſolution, though they have it not."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2f9fbd3a-5e80-4b9c-9891-605f9329e5ad",
                        "source_entry_id": "4b5ed373-2d13-34b0-aa04-7eca8f10dd5e",
                        "source_sense_id": "965c368d-3daa-322e-9ce1-cef938a7745d",
                        "target_lang_word": "penitent",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
